-- title:
--   Integral Eichler–Shimura eigenclass at level Nr
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O'$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain with the discrete valuation ring structure), let $N\ge 1$, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $H\le(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ be a subgroup. Let $g'$ be a nonzero cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$, let $A\subseteq\mathbb C$ be a subring, $\iota\colon A\to\mathcal O'$ an injective ring homomorphism, $b\colon\mathbb N\to A$ a family of coefficients, and $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ an arbitrary set of excluded indices. Assume that $g'$ is an eigenvector with eigenvalue $b(\ell)$ (viewed in $\mathbb C$) for the operator [`CuspForm.heckeTLin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) in weight $2$ for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, and an eigenvector with eigenvalue $b(q)$ for [`CuspForm.heckeULin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) in weight $2$ for every prime $q\mid N$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an additive homomorphism $v$ from $\mathrm{Additive}$ of $\Gamma_H(Nr)$ — the subgroup of $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ consisting of those elements of $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ whose lower-right entry modulo $Nr$ lies in $H$ — to $\mathcal O'$, such that: $v$ does not lie in the submodule $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O'}\cdot\top$ generated by the maximal ideal times the whole module; $v$ is parabolic, i.e. $v(\gamma)=0$ for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_H(Nr)$ whose matrix has trace squared equal to $4$; $\mathrm{heckeT}(Nr,H,\ell)v=\iota(b(\ell))\,v$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid Nr$ and $\ell\notin S$; $\mathrm{heckeT}(Nr,H,q)v=\iota(b(q))\,v$ for every prime $q\mid N$ (so the transfer-defined operator [`CohCarrier.heckeT`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250) is also used at the primes dividing the level, where one classically writes $U_q$, and no condition is imposed at $r$ itself); and $\langle d\rangle v=v$ for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$, the diamond operator [`CohCarrier.diamondL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55) acting by precomposition with conjugation by a chosen element of $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ of lower-right entry $d$.
--
--   This is the integral Eichler–Shimura realisation at an auxiliary level: a weight-two cuspidal eigenform on $\Gamma_0(N)$, with eigenvalues in a subring $A$ of $\mathbb C$ mapping into a discrete valuation ring, is converted into a primitive, parabolic, diamond-invariant class in the group-cohomological carrier $H^1(\Gamma_H(Nr),\mathcal O')$ carrying the same eigenvalues away from $S$. It feeds the construction of a level-raising point in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_subfamily_idempotentSplitting_point_level_mul_auxPrime`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_subfamily_idempotentSplitting_point_level_mul_auxPrime).
